┌ HADAL ── ARCHIVE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── LOGS 10/10  ── ACH 10/11 ┐
│ 1 SONAR   2 DESCENT  [3 ARCHIVE]  4 SYSTEM                                                       │
│LOGS                                                                                              │
│[01] You wake the console. The trench is already speaking.                                        │
│[02] A pulse leaves the hull. Something answers it with the same shape.                           │
│[03] The first hydrophone lowers into the dark and begins to drink the carrier.                   │
│[04] The carrier holds a band long enough to be a word. You write it down.                        │
│[05] BALLAST RELEASED. K-9 SINKS THROUGH ITS OWN SHADOW.                                          │
│[06] NINE THOUSAND METRES. The pressure writes on the hull in a language you almost read.         │
│[07] THE SIGNAL IS NO LONGER A SINGLE VOICE.                                                      │
│[08] A HUNDRED FATHOMS. Voss would have stopped here. You do not.                                 │
│[09] Every band has been tuned. The carrier is not a distress call. It is a rehearsal.            │
│[10] The station pulses without you now. It has learned the rhythm.                               │
